{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Arg","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Deriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.phase_sensitivity_times_frozen_displacement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.phase_sensitivity_times_frozen_displacement","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.lean#L127-L132","doc":"**The chain-rule crux (doubly zero after the correction).** The phase-channel\ncontribution `(∂S/∂φ)·Δφ` vanishes for two independent reasons: the displacement\n`Δφ = 0` (real anchors), and the sensitivity `∂S/∂φ|₀ = 0` (stationarity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.anchor_swing_is_magnitude_only","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.anchor_swing_is_magnitude_only","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.lean#L112-L125","doc":"**The corrected wall: the anchor-swing is pure magnitude.** At two real\nanchors the phase is `0` at both, and the bar-odd swing collapses to the\nmagnitude difference `(√3/2)·(rp² − rm²)` — the channel #4288 proved\nanchor-smooth. The phase contributes exactly nothing; and by\n`nzImVolume_phase_deriv` it could not contribute at first order even if\nperturbed. The sign flip is therefore out of reach of both smooth channels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.anchor_phase_difference_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.anchor_phase_difference_zero","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.lean#L106-L110","doc":"**Zero phase displacement between anchors** (unchanged). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.substrate_meridian_arg_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.substrate_meridian_arg_zero","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.lean#L97-L104","doc":"**The substrate freezes the phase** (unchanged by the correction). The\nsubstrate meridian coordinate is `u = 2·log q₀`, a nonnegative real for\n`q₀ ≥ 1`, so `arg(u) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.nzImVolume_phase_deriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.nzImVolume_phase_deriv","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.lean#L92-L95","doc":"`∂S/∂φ|₀ = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.nzImVolume_phase_hasDerivAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.nzImVolume_phase_hasDerivAt","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.lean#L77-L90","doc":"**Phase-sensitivity at `φ = 0` is ZERO (corrected).** The bar-odd face is\nstationary in the phase at the real ray — the old `√3·r²` slope was the\nRe-face's. Infinitesimal phase perturbations cannot move `S` at first order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.nzImVolume_quarter_turn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.nzImVolume_quarter_turn","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.lean#L71-L75","doc":"**The quarter turn lands on the diagonal zero.** `cos(π/2) = 0`: the\nspin-dominated regime `S < 0` begins only past the finite rotation `φ = π/4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.nzImVolume_phase_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.nzImVolume_phase_even","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.lean#L67-L69","doc":"The bar-odd face is even in the phase: `φ = 0` is a stationary point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.nzImVolume_real_ray","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.nzImVolume_real_ray","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.lean#L61-L65","doc":"**Real ray ⇒ bar-odd face maximal (corrected).** `cos 0 = 1`, so\n`S(r, 0) = (√3/2)·r²` — positive for `r ≠ 0`, not zero. The old `S = 0` claim\nwas the sin-quadrature bug. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.nzImVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.nzImVolume","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.lean#L56-L59","doc":"**Leading Neumann–Zagier bar-odd (Chern–Simons) face** in meridian polar\ncoordinates `(r, φ) = (|u|, arg u)`, corrected quadrature (bean `qou-u14x`):\n`S = (√3/2)·r²·cos(2φ)`, from `𝔙 = Vol + iκu²` (full-potential normalisation). ","signatureChunk":0}]}